/-!
# The per-output Gram prices `g_C` (UF661 data, LOCAL758/780 semantics)

For each squared output length `C < 1024` that occurs (854 values; the 170 values `4^a(8b+7)` have
no representative), `gTable C` is the largest complete squared row price over the representatives of
length `C`: tangent eigenvalue of the stored matrix plus the `10⁻⁷` allowance plus the analytic input
tail, rounded up on the `10⁻⁹` grid (reconstructed in `OddViscousNS_data/reports/gC_table.json`).
`gOVNS` extends it by the band-3 trace bound `.172754764` on `1024 ≤ C < 3600` and the analytic high
bound `.163043` for `C ≥ 3600`.  `RowBound gOVNS` is the finite-computation hypothesis of the forced
branch of Theorem 1.3 (the moment lemmas use the per-`C` prices); `gOVNS ≤ M₀` everywhere.
-/

